<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 1: Introduction to Mutual Funds (Weightage: 6%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
This foundational unit introduces the concept of mutual funds, their structural classification (open-ended, close-ended, interval funds), and investment objectives (equity, debt, hybrid, liquid). Candidates must understand the advantages of mutual funds and the specific role they play in the financial ecosystem.
</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 2: Legal Structure and Regulatory Framework (Weightage: 10%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
A highly critical chapter carrying a 10% weightage. Mutual funds in India are constituted as trusts. You must possess absolute clarity regarding the distinct roles and regulatory boundaries of the Sponsor, the Board of Trustees, the Asset Management Company (AMC), and the Custodian. Furthermore, you will be rigorously tested on the SEBI (Mutual Funds) Regulations, 1996.
</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 3: Roles and Responsibilities of RTAs in Mutual Funds (Weightage: 10%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
This section delves directly into your core job profile. It outlines the exhaustive responsibilities of an RTA, including maintaining the register of unit holders, processing corporate actions (like dividend payouts), and acting as the central hub for data transmission between the AMC, the distributor, and the investor. Practicing with our NISM II B Model Test modules ensures you memorise these specific operational workflows flawlessly.
</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 4: Investor Onboarding and KYC Process (Weightage: 8%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
Client onboarding is the first line of defence against financial fraud. This module requires mastery of the Know Your Customer (KYC) norms, Anti-Money Laundering (AML) guidelines, and the strict Foreign Account Tax Compliance Act (FATCA) / Common Reporting Standard (CRS) requirements. You must understand the role of KYC Registration Agencies (KRAs) and Central KYC (CKYC).
</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 5: Mutual Fund Transactions and Processes (Weightage: 12%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
Carrying the highest individual weightage (12%), this is the most operational chapter in the syllabus. You must understand the exact workflows for fresh purchases, additional purchases, redemptions, and scheme switches. It covers the validation of application forms, the verification of bank mandates, and the handling of rejected applications. A robust NISM II B Study Materials package is vital for mastering this procedural terminology.
</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 6: NAV, Pricing and Allotment of Units (Weightage: 10%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
The allocation of mutual fund units is strictly governed by the time the application and the funds are received. This chapter tests your knowledge of cut-off timings for liquid funds versus equity/debt funds. You must understand how Net Asset Value (NAV) is calculated, the impact of entry/exit loads, and the exact rules governing the applicability of historical versus prospective NAVs.
</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 7: Systematic Transactions (SIP, STP, SWP) (Weightage: 6%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
Systematic transactions form the bulk of retail mutual fund volumes. You must understand the registration, execution, and cancellation processes for Systematic Investment Plans (SIPs), Systematic Transfer Plans (STPs), and Systematic Withdrawal Plans (SWPs). The exam evaluates your knowledge of auto-debit mandates, NACH processes, and SIP pause facilities.


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 8: Investor Servicing and Grievance Redressal (Weightage: 10%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
RTAs are evaluated heavily on their service quality. This module covers the generation and dispatch of Consolidated Account Statements (CAS), handling requests for change of address or bank details, and the critical process of transmission of units upon the death of a unit holder. It also covers the SEBI SCORES portal for resolving investor complaints. Testing yourself with an NISM 2B Demo Test will solidify your understanding of statutory Turnaround Times (TAT) for these service requests.
</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 9: Compliance, Risk Management and Audit (Weightage: 10%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
Compliance is non-negotiable. This chapter covers the internal controls, risk management frameworks, and disaster recovery plans that an RTA must maintain. You will be tested on the frequency and scope of internal audits, SEBI inspections, and the severe regulatory penalties for operational negligence or data breaches.
</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 10: Record Maintenance and Reporting (Weightage: 8%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
RTAs must retain investor data and transaction records for specific durations as mandated by SEBI and PMLA. This section covers physical and electronic document storage, data security protocols, and the generation of Daily Transaction Reports (DTR) and compliance reports for the AMCs and Trustees.
</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 11: Taxation and Regulatory Reporting in Mutual Funds (Weightage: 5%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
While RTAs do not provide tax advice, they must deduct Tax Deducted at Source (TDS) for NRI investors and generate capital gains statements. Candidates must understand the fundamental taxation differences between equity-oriented and debt-oriented mutual funds, and the reporting of High-Value Transactions to the income tax authorities.
</p>


<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #094196;">Chapter 12: Technology and Operational Infrastructure in RTAs (Weightage: 5%)
</div>
<p style="color: #000; margin-top: 10px; text-align: justify;">
The final chapter explores the digital infrastructure of modern RTAs. It covers the use of application programming interfaces (APIs), the integration with payment gateways, cybersecurity protocols, and the technological platforms utilised by distributors to interface with RTA systems.
</p>

